{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++14 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++14 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cstring>\n#include <array>\n#include <vector>\n#include <numeric>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\nconst int MAXN = 33;\nusing Matrix = array<array<int, MAXN>, MAXN>;\nint SZ;\n\nMatrix id() {\n    Matrix C{};\n    for(int i=0;i<SZ;i++) C[i][i] = 1;\n    return C;\n}\n\nMatrix mul(const Matrix& A, const Matrix& B) {\n    static long long tmp[MAXN][MAXN];\n    memset(tmp, 0, sizeof(tmp));\n    const long long LIM = 8000000000000000000LL;\n    for(int k=0;k<SZ;k++)\n        for(int i=0;i<SZ;i++) {\n            int aik = A[i][k];\n            if(!aik) continue;\n            for(int j=0;j<SZ;j++) {\n                tmp[i][j] += 1LL * aik * B[k][j];\n                if(tmp[i][j] >= LIM) tmp[i][j] %= MOD;\n            }\n        }\n    Matrix C{};\n    for(int i=0;i<SZ;i++)\n        for(int j=0;j<SZ;j++)\n            C[i][j] = (int)(tmp[i][j] % MOD);\n    return C;\n}\n\nMatrix shift(const Matrix& A, int d) {\n    Matrix C{};\n    int K = SZ - 1;\n    for(int i=0;i<SZ;i++)\n        for(int j=0;j<SZ;j++) {\n            int ni = (i == K) ? K : (i + d) % K;\n            int nj = (j == K) ? K : (j + d) % K;\n            C[ni][nj] = A[i][j];\n        }\n    return C;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    int k;\n    scanf(\"%lld%d\", &n, &k);\n    SZ = k + 1;\n    vector<int> digits;\n    while(n) {\n        digits.push_back((int)(n % k));\n        n /= k;\n    }\n    vector<Matrix> pw(100, Matrix{});\n    for(int j=0;j<=k;j++) {\n        pw[0][0][j] = 1;\n        pw[0][j][j] = 1;\n    }\n    for(int i=1;i<(int)digits.size();i++) {\n        Matrix cur = id();\n        vector<int> idx(k);\n        iota(idx.begin(), idx.end(), 0);\n        cur = accumulate(idx.begin(), idx.end(), cur, [&](const Matrix& acc, int j) {\n            return mul(acc, shift(pw[i-1], j));\n        });\n        pw[i] = cur;\n    }\n    int add = 0;\n    Matrix ans = id();\n    for(int i=(int)digits.size()-1;i>=0;i--) {\n        for(int j=0;j<digits[i];j++)\n            ans = mul(ans, shift(pw[i], (j + add) % k));\n        add = (add + digits[i]) % k;\n    }\n    int ret = 0;\n    for(int i=0;i<=k;i++) {\n        ret += ans[i][k];\n        if(ret >= MOD) ret -= MOD;\n    }\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", ret);\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef id_matrix(sz):\n    C = [[0]*sz for _ in range(sz)]\n    for i in range(sz):\n        C[i][i] = 1\n    return C\n\ndef mul(A, B, sz):\n    # multiply two sz x sz matrices modulo MOD\n    # using temporary list of lists for intermediate sums\n    tmp = [[0]*sz for _ in range(sz)]\n    LIM = 8000000000000000000  # not needed in Python, but we keep logic similar\n    for k in range(sz):\n        for i in range(sz):\n            aik = A[i][k]\n            if aik == 0:\n                continue\n            for j in range(sz):\n                tmp[i][j] += aik * B[k][j]\n                # In Python we don't have overflow, but we can modulo later\n    C = [[0]*sz for _ in range(sz)]\n    for i in range(sz):\n        for j in range(sz):\n            C[i][j] = tmp[i][j] % MOD\n    return C\n\ndef shift(A, d, sz):\n    K = sz - 1\n    C = [[0]*sz for _ in range(sz)]\n    for i in range(sz):\n        for j in range(sz):\n            ni = K if i == K else (i + d) % K\n            nj = K if j == K else (j + d) % K\n            C[ni][nj] = A[i][j]\n    return C\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    sz = k + 1\n\n    # compute digits of n in base k (least significant first)\n    digits = []\n    temp = n\n    while temp > 0:\n        digits.append(temp % k)\n        temp //= k\n    if not digits:\n        digits = [0]  # n=0 case, but problem likely n>0\n\n    # precompute powers\n    pw = []\n    # pw[0]\n    base = [[0]*sz for _ in range(sz)]\n    for j in range(sz):\n        base[0][j] = 1\n        base[j][j] = 1\n    pw.append(base)\n\n    for i in range(1, len(digits)):\n        cur = id_matrix(sz)\n        for j in range(k):\n            cur = mul(cur, shift(pw[i-1], j, sz), sz)\n        pw.append(cur)\n\n    add = 0\n    ans = id_matrix(sz)\n    for i in range(len(digits)-1, -1, -1):\n        d = digits[i]\n        for j in range(d):\n            ans = mul(ans, shift(pw[i], (j + add) % k, sz), sz)\n        add = (add + d) % k\n\n    ret = 0\n    for i in range(sz):\n        ret += ans[i][k]\n        if ret >= MOD:\n            ret -= MOD\n    print(ret)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00012408917245920748, 0.0, 0.0, -0.00017808281700126827, -0.6413621306419373, -1.0847986231965479e-05, -0.0031827054917812347, -0.004079116974025965, -8.344646857949556e-07, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -5.173549288883805e-05, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.7418097943154862e-06, 0.0, -0.0024880189448595047, -5.00666465086